Here is the twenty-first system, focusing on high-stakes failures in the **Public Safety** sector. We are examining an **Emergency Dispatch API Gateway** used by a Computer-Aided Dispatch (CAD) system for E911 event injection.

For the vulnerabilities, we are focusing on **Pattern 8.2 (Fail-Open on Timeout)** combined with **Pattern 7.3 (Insufficient Logging of Critical Actions)**. This scenario demonstrates how a transient network failure (a 500ms timeout) causes the critical authentication layer to default to "allow," enabling an unauthenticated attacker to inject a false, high-priority emergency event, which then bypasses the internal audit logging system.

