Here is the twenty-fifth system, focusing on GraphQL-specific security failures. We are shifting into the **E-Commerce & Customer Profile Management** sector, focusing on a **Customer Identity & Profile GraphQL API**.

For the vulnerabilities, we are focusing on **Pattern 9.1 (GraphQL Mass Assignment / Vulerabilities in Operations)** combined with **Pattern 1.12 (Mass Assignment via Object Fields)**. This scenario demonstrates how a GraphQL mutation resolver accepts an input object and blindly maps it to the database model, allowing an attacker to inject an administrative field (`role: ADMIN`) to escalate their privileges in a single request.

